4067200,21.26],[1706745600,11.0],[1709251200,-3.33],[1711929600,1.43],[1714521600,-1.06],[1717200000,-28.34],[1719792000,-11.96],[1722470400,-11.39],[1725148800,14.75],[1727740800,3.16],[1730419200,29.86],[1733011200,25.91],[1735689600,5.23],[1738368000,-14.42],[1740787200,-5.63],[1743465600,7.63],[1746057600,6.68],[1748736000,13.24],[1751328000,14.56],[1754006400,33.24],[1756684800,8.13],[1759276800,14.22],[1761955200,56.55],[1764547200,15.8],[1767225600,22.89],[1769904000,36.35],[1772323200,10.87],[1775001600,23.22],[1777593600,11.17],[1780272000,25.31],[1782864000,28.1],[1785542400,0.84],[1788220800,13.75]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What is in each segment?","answer":"2W: motorcycles, scooters and mopeds (including electric). 3W: goods and passenger three-wheelers including e-rickshaws. PV: cars, utility vehicles and vans. CV: light, medium and heavy commercial vehicles and buses. Tractors: agricultural tractors (series starts January 2020 when FADA began reporting them)."},{"question":"How is this different from SIAM sales on this dashboard?","answer":"SIAM figures are manufacturer dispatches to dealers; FADA numbers are registrations to end customers. Over a few months they converge, but month to month dealer stocking (e.g. ahead of festivals or price changes) can make dispatch and retail diverge sharply - FADA's PV inventory-days commentary is the usual reconciling story."},{"question":"Caveats?","answer":"Months before 2022 had incomplete state coverage in FADA's releases, and the most recent month is preliminary and later releases restate earlier months upward (this series uses the restated year-ago figure from the following year's release where available, and fills gaps from the other comparison columns).^Gaps may exist where FADA published no release for a month and no later release carried it."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Values are VAHAN-based registrations ('retail') collated by FADA for the RTOs it can access; coverage of states changed over time (e.g. Telangana, Lakshadweep and some others were missing early on, Kerala added Dec 2019, Wheeled construction equipment added to the total in 2026), and FADA restates earlier months (by up to ~5-8 per cent in 2025-26) in later releases. To keep growth rates like-for-like, each month's own-release figure is replaced by the restated year-ago figure printed in the following year's release when one exists, so the latest 12 months are as first released and are likely to be revised up. The 'All vehicles' total includes tractors from Jan 2020 only.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:29:57+00:00"}